{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/schedule"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Systems\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"],"title":"Building and Running Schedules","generated":true,"anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A schedule holds the systems of one frame or step of a simulation. You build it by listing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the systems in a closure, and run it on a world with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which runs each system once:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 2, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","frame.run(on: &world)","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 4.0, y: 70.0)\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Ordering Systems","type":"heading","anchor":"Ordering-Systems","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order they’re written, except where an ordering constraint requires"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise. A system that must run after one written later, by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", or before one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written earlier, by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", is moved to satisfy the constraint, and every other system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its written place:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Scoring().after(Movement.self)","    Movement()","    Gravity().before(Movement.self)","}","print(frame.names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\", \"Scoring\"]\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A constraint naming a type with no system in the schedule is ignored, and one naming a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s own type doesn’t order the system against itself. Constraints that form a cycle,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so that no order satisfies them all, trap; build the schedule with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" to throw"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Running Systems at the Same Time","type":"heading","anchor":"Running-Systems-at-the-Same-Time","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two systems "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"conflict"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when one writes a type the other reads or writes, or when either has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":" runs conflicting systems in order and the rest at the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time. The world ends as though the systems had run one after another in order, except that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the commands systems queue apply when their wave finishes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, the order they run in rests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on how they happen to be written. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"reference"},{"text":" lists those pairs, so a test can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keep a schedule free of them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering"],"title":"Creating a Schedule","anchor":"Creating-a-Schedule"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runSerially(on:)"],"title":"Running Systems","anchor":"Running-Systems"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/after(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/before(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/inSet(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguous(with:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/docu